  "prediction": "The report provides an overview of 22 state Tax Credit Scholarship (TCS) programs in the United States. These programs enable low-income families to use tax credits to help pay for private school tuition. The report highlights key features of these programs, including eligibility criteria, funding limits, and tax credit percentages for individuals and businesses.\n\nThe eligibility criteria for these programs vary, with some being available only to individuals and others to both individuals and businesses. Funding limits also differ significantly, ranging from as low as $1,000 for individuals to over $500,000 for businesses. Tax credit percentages for individuals range from 2% of wages paid to 100% of tax liability, while for businesses, they range from 50% to 100% of tax liability.\n\nThe report also discusses the impact of TCS programs on state and local tax revenues and the potential federal tax implications for donors. It is important to note that the report does not provide an exhaustive list of all state TCS programs or their specific rules and regulations.\n\nIn summary, the report offers valuable insights into the design and implementation of TCS programs across the United States, highlighting their eligibility criteria, funding limits, and tax credit percentages for individuals and businesses. It also touches upon the potential federal tax implications for donors.",
  "scored_prediction": "The report provides an overview of 22 state Tax Credit Scholarship (TCS) programs in the United States. These programs enable low-income families to use tax credits to help pay for private school tuition. The report highlights key features of these programs, including eligibility criteria, funding limits, and tax credit percentages for individuals and businesses.\n\nThe eligibility criteria for these programs vary, with some being available only to individuals and others to both individuals and businesses. Funding limits also differ significantly, ranging from as low as $1,000 for individuals to over $500,000 for businesses. Tax credit percentages for individuals range from 2% of wages paid to 100% of tax liability, while for businesses, they range from 50% to 100% of tax liability.\n\nThe report also discusses the impact of TCS programs on state and local tax revenues and the potential federal tax implications for donors. It is important to note that the report does not provide an exhaustive list of all state TCS programs or their specific rules and regulations.\n\nIn summary, the report offers valuable insights into the design and implementation of TCS programs across the United States, highlighting their eligibility criteria, funding limits, and tax credit percentages for individuals and businesses. It also touches upon the potential federal tax implications for donors.",
